    "explanation": "1. CONCEPT:\nThe first law of limiting friction states that the limiting friction $f_{\\text{lim}}$ is directly proportional to the normal reaction $N$ between the contacting surfaces: $f_{\\text{lim}} \\propto N \\implies f_{\\text{lim}} = \\mu_s N$.\n\n2. GIVEN:\nLaws of limiting friction.\n\n3. FORMULA / PRINCIPLE:\n$f_{\\text{lim}} = \\mu_s N$.\n\n4. STEP-BY-STEP SOLUTION:\n1. Limiting friction arises from microscopic contact asperities that weld together under normal compression.\n2. Greater normal force compresses these microscopic peaks, increasing true contact area.\n3. Hence, limiting friction increases linearly with the normal reaction $N$.\n4. It is independent of the apparent macroscopic surface area.\n\n5. FINAL ANSWER:\nOption A: The normal reaction between the contact surfaces\n\n6. QUICK TIP:\nLimiting friction $\\propto N$. It is independent of the apparent surface area of contact!",
