      "stepByStep": "1. Total length of incline is $L$. The block starts at rest at the top ($K_i = 0$) and stops at the bottom ($K_f = 0$).\n2. By the work-energy theorem: $\\Delta K = W_{\\text{total}} = 0$.\n3. Work done by gravity along the entire length $L$:\n   $W_g = (mg\\sin\\theta) L$.\n4. Friction acts only over the bottom half of length $L/2$:\n   $W_f = -(f_k) \\left(\\frac{L}{2}\\right) = -(\\mu_k mg\\cos\\theta) \\left(\\frac{L}{2}\\right)$.\n5. Setting total work to zero:\n   $mg L\\sin\\theta - \\mu_k mg\\cos\\theta \\frac{L}{2} = 0$.\n6. Dividing by $mg L\\cos\\theta$:\n   $\\tan\\theta - \\frac{\\mu_k}{2} = 0 \\implies \\mu_k = 2\\tan\\theta$.",
